    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "about",
      "title": "Note",
      "uuid": "e5f7d7e4d6e8409190f1d65f99d26b22",
      "x": 1245.9083718527545,
      "y": -328.2755974440369,
      "width": 96.69470981289624,
      "height": 26.93495272105457,
      "z_value": 10.0,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": false,
      "label": "Elegant",
      "depth_front": true,
      "node_tint": ""
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "claude_response",
      "title": "Response",
      "uuid": "553a238b598044dc82bd28efd9b699d4",
      "x": -999999.0,
      "y": -999999.0,
      "width": 420.0,
      "height": 316.0,
      "z_value": 0.0,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": true,
      "label": "Found it. `NW` and `NH` are floats from `rect().width()/height()`, so `max(NW, NH) // 2` is also a float \u2014 and `range()` rejects float arguments with a `TypeError`, which swallows the whole spawn silently. The node was being created at -999,999 and abandoned there.",
      "depth_front": false,
      "node_tint": ""
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "about",
      "title": "Note",
      "uuid": "15185011d72d406883f39b66cc3d0a63",
      "x": 1431.5622163825396,
      "y": -738.7300643487749,
      "width": 74.18820508500175,
      "height": 26.934952721054515,
      "z_value": 10.0,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": false,
      "label": "Grace",
      "depth_front": true,
      "node_tint": ""
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "image",
      "title": "Image",
      "uuid": "4cb902c9cff44d35b787dda4b64be5e0",
      "x": 1963.0,
      "y": 133.67161204180888,
      "width": 298.0,
      "height": 310.0,
      "z_value": 0.0,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": false,
      "image_b64": "",
      "cache_key": "28d9a3da153ae2e7c52081bf02e4a10a8e3276b9abec98817cf3597e5ad3fdc2",
      "caption": "City skyline with light trails",
      "source_path": "C:\\Users\\thisg\\Desktop\\A Charm in the shape of an Expressed Emotion\\Images\\downloadedImage (10).png",
      "source_size": 2004582,
      "source_mtime": 1771066851.5372534,
      "show_border": true,
      "depth_front": false
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "claude_response",
      "title": "Response",
      "uuid": "bb22916f68914b20aeb80bed5a25fab9",
      "x": -999999.0,
      "y": -999999.0,
      "width": 420.0,
      "height": 176.0,
      "z_value": 0.0,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": true,
      "label": "Let me read the current state of the function to see what actually got written:",
      "depth_front": false,
      "node_tint": ""
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "claude_response",
      "title": "Response",
      "uuid": "654d8caf0a21459fb54a0a797cd66035",
      "x": -999999.0,
      "y": -999999.0,
      "width": 420.0,
      "height": 428.0,
      "z_value": 0.0,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": true,
      "label": "The bug is in `_clear`. `QGraphicsItem` itself has a `data(key)` method, so `hasattr(item, 'data')` is `True` for **every** item in the scene \u2014 including Port ellipses, which also have `rect()` from `QGraphicsEllipseItem`. Every probe hits a port and returns `False`, so nothing ever spawns.\n\nFix: check `isinstance` against `BaseNode` instead:",
      "depth_front": false,
      "node_tint": ""
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "claude_response",
      "title": "Response",
      "uuid": "709f72ee0fee4d32b84e93c33db397db",
      "x": -999999.0,
      "y": -999999.0,
      "width": 420.0,
      "height": 596.0,
      "z_value": 0.0,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": true,
      "label": "Done. What persists across restarts:\n\n- `ui.preview_pinned = true/false` \u2014 whether the panel is pinned\n- `ui.preview_pinned_path = \"/abs/path/to/image.jpg\"` \u2014 which image was pinned, matched by `source_path`\n\nOn startup, after the session loads, `_restore_pinned_preview` walks the scene, finds the `ImageNode` with the matching path, loads its pixmap into the panel, and silently re-engages the pin button (via `blockSignals` so it doesn't re-trigger the save unnecessarily). If the image node is no longer on the canvas the pin simply doesn't restore.",
      "depth_front": false,
      "node_tint": ""
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "claude_response",
      "title": "Response",
      "uuid": "b8093edd8bb847378cacf39e5d85e881",
      "x": -999999.0,
      "y": -999999.0,
      "width": 420.0,
      "height": 148.0,
      "z_value": 0.0,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": true,
      "label": "Now call `_restore_pinned_preview` after the session loads:",
      "depth_front": false,
      "node_tint": ""
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "claude_response",
      "title": "Response",
      "uuid": "21fd556d31f848c8babad4e94e0287c5",
      "x": -999999.0,
      "y": -999999.0,
      "width": 420.0,
      "height": 288.0,
      "z_value": 0.0,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": true,
      "label": "Clear picture. I'll:\n1. Save `preview_pinned` + `preview_pinned_path` when pin toggles\n2. Add `_restore_pinned_preview()` called after session loads (deferred so nodes are in the scene)\n3. Clear the saved pin when unpinning",
      "depth_front": false,
      "node_tint": ""
    },
    {
